xgis 1

/* OpenFreeMap "Bright" — live one-line import.
 *
 * The runtime fetches the style.json, sniffs its Mapbox v8 shape
 * (`version` + `layers`), runs convertMapboxStyle, and renders the
 * FULL style — all sources (openmaptiles planet tilejson + ne2 raster)
 * AND the symbol layers (place/POI/road-name/shield labels).
 *
 * This replaces a hand-converted static snapshot that was generated
 * before symbol→label conversion existed: it had EVERY `label_*` /
 * `poi_*` / `highway-name` / `highway-shield` / `airport` layer dropped
 * with a "type=symbol unsupported" note, so the scene loaded with no
 * labels at all. The current converter supports those, so importing
 * live brings the complete real-world map back — which is what we want
 * to stress-test pitched / panned mobile views against.
 *
 * Navigate to a city: #14/35.68/139.76 (Tokyo), #14/40.78/-73.97 (Manhattan).
 */

import "https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/bright"
